@bank all
// Pillar 5 (head writer, seat W): head-scratcher texts (seat H's case engine, 24k) and the Chief's notes. TEXTS.
// {machine} the machine's name, {shows} its card, {part} a part.

== case.tab.notes
- Fault notes
== case.tab.chief
- The Chief's notes
== case.title
- Head-scratcher: {machine} {shows}.
== case.suspects
- Suspects
== case.notes
- Notes
== case.cross
- Cross off
== case.uncross
- Put back
== case.call
- Call it: {part}?
== case.where
- Where next?
== case.hint.p3.1
- Have you read every note? One's on the machine.
// case.solved: shown only AFTER the fix works (the machine is right again), never at "Call it", so it can't give the answer away
== case.solved
- Fixed. That was it.
== case.wrong
- Not that one. Have another look at the notes.
== case.new
- A new head-scratcher is on the board.

// The Chief's notes, page 1: "What's been tried" (three lines, Calder's hand)
== chief.p3.title
- What's been tried
== chief.p3.1
- If someone fitted it and it's still wrong, it isn't that.
== chief.p3.2
- Read every note. They're not all on the card. Check the machine.
== chief.p3.3
- The scanner sees what's worn. The notes see what's been tried.
